WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
The United Nations is warning that hunger is about to get worse in 16 places around the world.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:12.160
The UN food agencies say acute food insecurity is expected to deteriorate between December and next May.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:20.080
In 16 hotspots, up from 13 in June, Sudan, South Sudan, Somalia, Northern Nigeria,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.520
and Yemen face the gravest threats, with a risk of famine in parts of Sudan through January.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.440
Conflict is driving hunger in 12 of the 16 hotspots.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.400
A strengthening El Niño, possibly one of the strongest on record, threatens harvests in

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:40.080
Southern Africa and Central America, where the first crop season was the driest in four decades.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:46.720
In Guatemala alone, over 3 million people are projected to face high levels of acute food insecurity.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:53.040
Funding for food assistance in the five worst-hit countries has fallen 62% since 2022.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.040
The agencies say early action can still prevent the worst outcomes,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.920
but only if the money and safe access follow.

